      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I have all the information I need. This is a single problem (problem 14) about expected value.\n\n**Problem analysis:**\n- 5 balls labeled 1–5, drawn with replacement 3 times.\n- $X$ = number of distinct balls that appear at least once.\n- Find $E(X)$.\n\n**Solution using indicator variables:**\nLet $X_i = 1$ if ball $i$ is drawn at least once, else 0. Then $X = \\sum_{i=1}^{5} X_i$.\n\n$P(X_i = 0) = (4/5)^3 = 64/125$, so $P(X_i = 1) = 1 - 64/125 = 61/125$.\n\n$E(X_i) = 61/125$.\n\n$E(X) = 5 \\times 61/125 = 305/125 = 61/25 = 2.44$.\n\nLet me verify with an alternative method: $E(X) = \\sum_{k} k \\cdot P(X=k)$.\n- $P(X=1) = 5 \\cdot (1/5)^3 = 5/125 = 1/25$\n- $P(X=2) = \\binom{5}{2} \\cdot \\frac{2^3 - 2}{5^3} = 10 \\cdot 6/125 = 60/125$\n- $P(X=3) = \\binom{5}{3} \\cdot \\frac{3!}{5^3} = 10 \\cdot 6/125 = 60/125$\n- Sum: $5/125 + 120/125 + 180/125 = 305/125 = 61/25$ ✓",
        "tool_calls": [
